index 0000000..83b6eed
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/repository_client_contract.md
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Repository-owned client companion contract
+
+Stage 4 extends merged PR #1 at
+`0dd5d2225e2d093f66a4b6231c1aa35004f2c8f3` on `client_centric_repo`.
+The Lean toolchain and Mathlib deployment pin remain unchanged.
+
+`protocol.describe {}` identifies `maths-ai-pantograph`, protocol version 2,
+model S-expression version 1, transition validation version 1, message version 1,
+`explicit-focused-v1` goal selection, and `string-array-v1` tactic errors.
+Version 2 adds transition provenance, `goal.inspect` and `goal.certify`; see
+[snapshot_protocol.md](snapshot_protocol.md).
+The planning document's contract revision 2 is not a runtime compatibility mode.
+
+Successful `goal.tactic` responses retain `nextStateId`, `goals`, `messages`,
+`hasSorry`, and `hasUnsafe`. They also carry
+`validation: {version: 1, scope: "transition-expressions", checked: true}`.
+The metadata states that the defined expression checks completed. A positive
+admission or unsafe flag remains a successful allocation for the client to delete
+before rejecting that candidate. Missing or cyclic evidence returns a command
+error with category `validation` and allocates no result state.
+
+The shared operation transaction captures diagnostics and restores its caller's
+meta, elaborator, environment, message, trace, information, and declaration-cache
+state. Fresh-name counters remain monotonic. Logged errors reject execution even
+when tactics return normally. Thrown errors retain their diagnostics. Warnings
+and information survive success. Tagged messages retain their kind. Source
+strings use their real source maps; unavailable positions are exactly `(0, 0)`.
+Snapshot serialization and diagnostics also restore their caller.
+
+The parser runs full tactic or conversion sequences with end-of-input checking.
+Deferred synthetic elaboration runs inside the transaction. Default synthesis
+resolves ordinary implicit arguments. Partial synthesis runs deferred tactics
+while permitting unresolved typeclass obligations. Reachable unresolved holes
+remain goals. This applies to goal initialization as well as subsequent operations.
+
+Validation inspects the selected goal, input and returned goals, new or changed
+ordinary and delayed assignments, new local contexts, and pending synthetic
+expressions. It follows ordinary assignments and delayed pending assignments,
+local types and values, constant dependencies, and projection dependencies.
+Admission scanning uses elaborated terms rather than tactic strings. Unsafe
+scanning concerns resulting proof dependencies rather than the implementation
+of the tactic elaborator.
+
+Each state retains its original trust environment. Dependency traversal stops at
+that environment but still checks directly referenced constants for unsafe status.
+New reachable declarations have their types and values scanned recursively,
+including declarations retained from earlier transitions. Imported Mathlib
+remains the trust basis. This does not audit all imported axioms or kernel-certify
+an assembled theorem reconstructed from independent search nodes.
+
+Safety scanning covers changed assignments even when they are no longer visible.
+Obligation retention follows the selected, input and returned goals and their
+reachable expressions. Discarded elaboration variables are not all promoted to
+user goals. Existing dormant siblings retain manual-mode behavior. A retained
+conversion equation owns its evolving right-hand placeholders until conversion
+exit; unresolved holes after exit remain obligations. Cyclic expression
+assignments and missing declarations fail validation.
+
+All existing structured operations use the shared transaction: assignment,
+have/let/define, calc, motivated application, no-confusion, and conversion
+entry/exit. The merged omitted-index default, nonzero selection, sibling resumption,
+mode metadata and automatic final-conversion exit remain supported. Repeated
+references to the same resumed goal are removed while preserving order.
+
+The model serializer's expression normalization, fields, binder roles and local
+indices are unchanged. Its snapshot reads now restore their caller. Complete
+sequence parsing and synthetic elaboration can change fresh internal names;
+normalized expressions, graph fingerprints, node features and edges retain their
+canonical meaning.
+
+Verification: `lake build repl Test.ContractFixtures` and `lake test` pass.
+The suite contains 299 assertions, including 37 Stage 4 assertions. Existing
+Python codec, reconciliation, environment and model tests report 316 passes.
+The final diagnostic records 61 raw Mathlib exchanges against the existing codec,
+four unchanged canonical graph goldens, zero final allocations, and confirmed
+subprocess reaping. The sandboxed diagnostic's shutdown timeout is not counted
+as a pass; the recorded final capture ran outside that sandbox.
+
+The tracked patch, source hashes, executable hash and live evidence are in
+`pantograph_backport/`. The build reused a copied archive dependency/build cache
+and rebuilt changed targets. Stage 7's fresh release reproduction remains pending.
+Stage 5 actual-client integration, Stage 6 production migration, and Stage 8
+RL/deployment validation remain pending. No fork publication, dependency migration
+or RL launch is part of Stage 4.
diff --git a/doc/snapshot_protocol.md b/doc/snapshot_protocol.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d853f12
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/snapshot_protocol.md
@@ -0,0 +1,117 @@
+# Retained snapshots: provenance, inspection and certification
+
+Protocol version 2 lets a client keep result states alive and run later
+tactics on them directly, instead of rebuilding each goal from its printed
+form. It adds what such a client needs: how a transition's goals relate to its
+input, a read-only view of obligations a state no longer lists, and a kernel
+check of a complete root proof.
+
+`protocol.describe` reports `protocolVersion: 2` together with
+`transitionProvenanceVersion: 1`, `inspectionVersion: 1` and
+`certificationVersion: 1`. The model S-expression version stays 1, and model
+goal serialization is unchanged.
+
+Names below are metavariable and free-variable IDs (`_uniq.N`). They identify
+an obligation or local inside one state lineage. They are not stable across
+sessions or across a replay of the same tactics, and a client must not persist
+them.
+
+## Transition provenance
+
+Every successful `goal.tactic` response carries `transition`:
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `selected` | The input goal the operation ran on |
+| `direct` | Unassigned goals the operation produced for `selected`, in the order the tactic returned them, before automatic resumption |
+| `introduced` | One list per `direct` goal: its visible locals that `selected` does not have, in context order |
+| `siblings` | Input goals other than `selected` that the result still lists |
+| `changed` | The siblings whose instantiated target, or a local type or value, differs from the input |
+| `closed` | Input goals other than `selected` that the transition assigned |
+| `dormant` | Input goals other than `selected` that are unassigned but not listed |
+| `extra` | Every other listed goal, such as a reachable hole restored by validation |
+
+`direct`, `siblings` and `extra` partition `goals`. A goal the tactic returned
+that was already an input goal counts as a sibling, not as a direct goal. If the
+operation leaves `selected` itself open, as `skip` does, `selected` is its own
+only direct goal. The
+categories come from metavariable identities and assignments in the saved
+contexts, never from comparing printed goals.
+
+After `constructor` on `True ∧ True`, both goals are direct. Solving the second
+of them gives `selected` = that goal, no direct goals, and the first goal as a
+sibling. With `∃ n : Nat, n = 0 ∧ n = 1` split into `?w`, `?a` and `?b`, solving
+`?a` with `rfl` assigns the witness: `?w` is closed and `?b` is changed.
+
+## `goal.inspect`
+
+Request `{"stateId", "goals"}`, where `goals` is a nonempty list of distinct
+obligation names. The response lists one entry per name, in request order:
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `name` | The obligation |
+| `status` | `active` (listed), `pending` (unassigned, not listed), `assigned` (assigned, with unresolved holes), `delayed` (delayed assignment whose pending proof has unresolved holes) or `complete` |
+| `goal` | The serialized goal, for `active` and `pending` |
+| `holes` | Unassigned metavariables reachable from the instantiated target and locals, or from the instantiated assignment |
+| `universeHoles` | Whether a universe metavariable remains |
+
+An obligation is `complete` when its instantiated assignment has no
+metavariables, including universe ones. A name the state does not declare is an
+`index` error. Inspection changes no state and allocates nothing.
+
+## `goal.certify`
+
+Request `{"stateId"}` with optional `maxHeartbeats` (thousands, as the Lean
+option; default 200000). The response is `{version, status, reason?, receipt?}`:
+
+| `status` | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `certified` | The kernel accepted the root proof; `receipt` is present |
+| `incomplete` | Goals remain, the root is unassigned, or holes remain |
+| `rejected` | The proof is not acceptable; `reason` says why |
+| `inconclusive` | The kernel ran out of heartbeats, memory or recursion depth, or was interrupted |
+
+The server records the root statement and its universe parameters at
+`goal.start`. Certification:
+
+1. requires an empty goal list and an assigned root, then instantiates the root
+   assignment and requires it to be free of term and universe metavariables;
+2. abstracts the proof over the root's local context natively (assumptions
+   become binders, local definitions keep their values) and rejects loose bound
+   variables or locals outside that context;
+3. checks the proof against the recorded root statement, not the root's
+   current type and not any caller-supplied statement;
+4. walks every constant the proof reaches, imported ones included, and rejects
+   `sorryAx`, unsafe dependencies, missing declarations and axioms that are not
+   in the state's trusted environment;
+5. rechecks declarations added during the search (auxiliary lemmas, matchers)
+   in dependency order on a copy of the trusted environment, then checks the
+   root as a theorem (or, for a statement that is not a proposition, as an
+   opaque definition) with `Environment.addDeclCore`. The kernel is called
+   directly, so `debug.skipKernelTC` cannot skip checking.
+
+Checking works on environment values only. No search state, and not the REPL's
+own environment, sees the temporary declaration, and certifying again returns
+the same result.
+
+The receipt records the root name, universe parameters, a structural 64-bit
+digest of the checked statement and proof (`identity: lean-expr-digest-v1`,
+which ignores bound variable names, so a term is identified up to renaming),
+an identity of the trusted environment (toolchain commit and imported module
+names), the Lean version, the baseline axioms the proof uses and the
+auxiliary declarations that were rechecked. It is reproducibility metadata. It
+is not a cryptographic proof, and it does not replace rechecking a replayed
+proof in a fresh session.
+
+## Tests
+
+`Test/Snapshot.lean` covers nonzero selection, either side of a conjunction
+first, identical targets, survivors next to direct goals, introduced locals,
+the shared witness (closed and changed siblings, separate alternatives),
+inspection of solved and delayed obligations, and rejected inspection requests.
+For certification it covers incomplete states, repeated checks, the
+conflicting witness, universe-polymorphic roots, reported baseline axioms, a
+new axiom, a rechecked auxiliary lemma, new and trusted-basis admissions, an
+ill-typed assignment under `debug.skipKernelTC=true`, and a replaced root
+statement.
diff --git a/scripts/capture_repository_client_contract.py b/scripts/capture_repository_client_contract.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..925b77b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/capture_repository_client_contract.py
@@ -0,0 +1,220 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Capture Stage 4 wire evidence and check it against the existing application codec.
+
+Run with the application's Python environment. Output must be a new directory.
+Historical captures are read as replay inputs and are never modified.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+import asyncio
+import hashlib
+import json
+import os
+from pathlib import Path
+import subprocess
+import sys
+
+BASE = "0dd5d2225e2d093f66a4b6231c1aa35004f2c8f3"
+
+
+async def capture(args):
+    repo = args.repo.resolve()
+    application = args.application.resolve()
+    fixtures = application / "maths_ai/gnn_inference/tests/fixtures/pantograph"
+    sys.path.insert(0, str(application))
+    from maths_ai.hybrid_reasoner.pantograph_protocol import (
+        decode_json_response, decode_response, decode_execution_goal,
+    )
+    from maths_ai.gnn_inference.atp_lean_gnn.graph import dag_fingerprint, model_goal_to_dag
+
+    assert subprocess.check_output(["git", "rev-parse", "HEAD"], cwd=repo, text=True).strip() == BASE
+    toolchain = (repo / "lean-toolchain").read_text().strip()
+    assert toolchain == (args.mathlib / "lean-toolchain").read_text().strip()
+    env = os.environ.copy()
+    mathlib_path = subprocess.check_output(
+        ["lake", "env", "printenv", "LEAN_PATH"], cwd=args.mathlib, text=True,
+    ).strip()
+    own_path = subprocess.check_output(
+        ["lake", "env", "printenv", "LEAN_PATH"], cwd=repo, text=True,
+    ).strip()
+    # Lake may return relative package paths; resolve them against each owning project.
+    def absolute_paths(value, owner):
+        return os.pathsep.join(str((owner / p).resolve()) if not Path(p).is_absolute() else p
+                               for p in value.split(os.pathsep) if p)
+    env["LEAN_PATH"] = absolute_paths(own_path, repo) + os.pathsep + absolute_paths(mathlib_path, args.mathlib)
+    repl = repo / ".lake/build/bin/repl"
+    proc = await asyncio.create_subprocess_exec(
+        "stdbuf", "-oL", str(repl), "Mathlib", "Test.ContractFixtures",
+        cwd=repo, env=env, stdin=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE,
+        stdout=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE, stderr=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE,
+    )
+    stderr_task = asyncio.create_task(proc.stderr.read())
+    entries = []
+    allocated = set()
+    graph_checks = []
+    try:
+        ready = (await asyncio.wait_for(proc.stdout.readline(), 30)).decode().rstrip("\n")
+        assert ready == "ready.", ready
+
+        async def call(label, command, payload, *, owned=True):
+            line = command + " " + json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":"))
+            proc.stdin.write((line + "\n").encode())
+            await proc.stdin.drain()
+            response_line = (await asyncio.wait_for(proc.stdout.readline(), 30)).decode().rstrip("\n")
+            response = decode_json_response(response_line)
+            if owned:
+                decode_response(command, response)
+            entries.append(dict(label=label, command=command, request=payload,
+                                request_line=line, response_line=response_line, response=response))
+            for key in ("stateId", "nextStateId"):
+                if key in response:
+                    allocated.add(response[key])
+            if command == "goal.delete":
+                allocated.difference_update(payload["stateIds"])
+            return response
+
+        upstream = json.loads((fixtures / "upstream_pr1/capture.json").read_text())
+        golden = json.loads((fixtures / "canonical_graph_expectations.json").read_text())["goals"]
+        id_map = {}
+        renames = {
+            "unsupported_descriptor": "descriptor",
+            "admission_flag_present_without_validation": "checked_admission",
+            "logged_error_still_succeeds_without_diagnostics": "logged_error_rejected",
+        }
+        for old in upstream["interactions"]:
+            payload = dict(old["request"])
+            if "stateId" in payload:
+                payload["stateId"] = id_map.get(payload["stateId"], payload["stateId"])
+            if "stateIds" in payload:
+                payload["stateIds"] = sorted(allocated)
+            label = renames.get(old["label"], old["label"])
+            result = await call(label, old["command"], payload)
+            for key in ("stateId", "nextStateId"):
+                if key in old["response"] and key in result:
+                    id_map[old["response"][key]] = result[key]
+            if label in golden:
+                actual = result["goals"]
+                expected = golden[label]
+                assert len(actual) == len(expected)
+                for wire, target in zip(actual, expected):
+                    goal = decode_execution_goal(wire).goal
+                    canonical = goal.model_dump()
+                    assert canonical == target["canonical"], (label, canonical, target["canonical"])
+                    assert goal.state_fingerprint() == target["state_fingerprint"]
+                    dag = model_goal_to_dag(goal)
+                    assert dag_fingerprint(dag) == target["dag_fingerprint"]
+                    assert [node.as_dict() for node in dag.nodes] == target["nodes"]
+                    assert [list(edge) for edge in dag.edges] == target["edges"]
+                    assert dag.expression_root_id == target["expression_root_id"]
+                    assert dag.state_root_id == target["state_root_id"]
+                graph_checks.append(label)
+            if label == "logged_error_rejected":
+                assert result.get("tacticErrors") == ["capture error"]
+                assert "nextStateId" not in result
+                assert result["messages"][0]["data"] == "capture error"
+
+        root = (await call("validation_start", "goal.start", {"expr": "True"}))["stateId"]
+        for label, text, flag in [
+            ("skip", "skip", None),
+            ("warning_info", 'run_tac Lean.logWarning "warning evidence"\nrun_tac Lean.logInfo "information evidence"\ntrivial', None),
+            ("tagged_warning", "contract_tagged_warning", None),
+            ("nested_admission", "exact (by sorry)", "hasSorry"),
+            ("local_admission", "have h : True := by sorry\nexact h", "hasSorry"),
+            ("introduced_dependency_admission", "contract_dependency_sorry", "hasSorry"),
+            ("positive_unsafe", "contract_unsafe", "hasUnsafe"),
+            ("hidden_hole", "contract_hidden_hole", None),
+            ("delayed_hole", "contract_delayed_hole", None),
+            ("hidden_local_value", "contract_hidden_local_value", None),
+            ("missing_assignment", "contract_missing_assignment", "validation"),
+            ("failed_snapshot_mutation", "contract_failed_mutation", "failure"),
+            ("reuse_after_failure", "trivial", None),
+            ("trailing_input", "trivial\nthis_is_not_a_tactic", "parse"),
+        ]:
+            result = await call(label, "goal.tactic", {"stateId": root, "goalId": 0, "tactic": text})
+            if flag in ("hasSorry", "hasUnsafe"):
+                assert result[flag] is True and result["validation"]["checked"] is True
+            elif flag == "failure":
